course: dictionary
lesson: 3465
title: Fairness: treating everyone equally
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fairness is a noun. It means treating people equally and justly, following the rules, and not cheating or favouring anyone. You will meet it at school, in stories and in games.
explain: Look at the words around it. «If you see a friend cheat, loyalty and fairness clash» tells you fairness is something that can pull against loyalty, like when a friend breaks the rules. «Fairness includes sharing the broken or boring things, not only the fun ones» shows that being fair means sharing the dull jobs too.
explain: Fair does not always mean the same. Fairness can mean everyone gets what they need. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Fairness to all» means treating everybody justly, and that fits.
explain: Fairness has an old meaning too: pale skin or light hair. You will rarely see this today, so when you meet it in an old book, the context will tell you which meaning the author means.
fact: Fairness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some fairness, not a fairness.
fact: «Fairness» means treating people equally and justly, and not favouring anyone.
fact: In maths, fair sharing means dividing something into equal parts.
fact: A fair coin or dice gives every result an equal chance of happening.
fact: Phrases to know include «a sense of fairness» and «fairness to all»; in an old story, fairness may mean pale skin or light hair.
exercise: «Fairness includes sharing the broken or boring things, not only the fun ones.» What does fairness mean here? | *Treating everyone equally, even with the dull jobs | Being quiet during lessons | Having pale skin | Winning every game
exercise: Two children share a cake: one cuts, and the other chooses first. Why does this help fairness? | The cake gets bigger | *The cutter wants equal pieces, because the other child picks first | The cutter gets the biggest piece every time | Nobody needs to share at all
exercise: You see a friend cheat. What does the example say is often a good first step? | Tell the whole class at once | Copy them so you are not left out | *Talk to your friend | Ignore it and say nothing ever
test: What does «fairness» mean in a game where everyone takes turns? | *Treating everyone equally and following the rules | Being loud and bossy | Going first every time | Winning the most points
test: Which of these is the noun form of fair? | unfairly | *fairness | fairly | fairer
exam: Sam says fairness means getting the biggest share. Why is Sam wrong? | Fairness means having pale skin | *Fairness means treating people equally and justly, not getting the most | Fairness means nobody ever shares anything | Fairness means being first in every line
